# Cursor Rules for Python Meijer Project

This project follows specific development rules and best practices. All rules are defined in the `.cursor/rules/` directory.

## Rule Categories

- **log_handling.mdc**: Rules for handling mitmproxy logs and binary files
- **no_git_reset.mdc**: Git operations and commit requirements
- **no_home_rm.mdc**: File deletion safety rules
- **no_sudo.mdc**: System operations and privilege restrictions
- **plaintext_tools.mdc**: Proper tool selection for different file types
- **python_venv.mdc**: Python virtual environment requirements

## General Guidelines

- Follow all rules defined in the `.cursor/rules/` directory
- Use appropriate tools for each file type
- Maintain security best practices
- Follow Python development standards
- Use proper git workflow with commits and pushes

## Project-Specific Rules

- All Python development uses virtual environments (`venv`)
- Never use system pip or install packages system-wide
- Use proper tools for mitmproxy log analysis
- Follow detailed commit message format with technical attribution
- Maintain proper file safety practices
